# ==============================================================================
# File: .gitignore
# Purpose: Prevents sensitive credentials, local environment overrides, runtime
#          audit logs, backup policy snapshots, and OS/IDE artifacts from being
#          committed to version control inside `New/agy-config/`.
# Architecture/Context: Enforces secret hygiene for workstation MDM policy
#          templates and deployment scripts before packaging for Jamf, Intune,
#          Ansible, FleetDM, or Google Cloud storage buckets.
# Dependencies/Side Effects: Git SCM ignore rules; `!.env.example` and
#          `!settings.env` remain tracked as safe configuration templates.
# ==============================================================================

# 1. Environment Overrides & Secrets (CRITICAL — Never Commit Live Keys)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local.json
*.secret.json
*secret*
!configs/07-security-guard-scripts/*

# 2. Certificates, Private Keys & Cloud Service Account Credentials
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json
gcloud-key.json

# 3. Runtime Security Hook Logs & Policy Backup Snapshots
*.log
agy_security_audit.log
*.bak
*.backup
*.orig
*.tmp
*.corrupted.*

# 4. Packaged MDM Bundles & Build Artifacts
dist/
build/
out/
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.pkg
*.intunewin

# 5. Operating System & Editor / IDE Noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
